        "Large-number handling and storing a summary are optional extensions. Running the example with explicit outcome comparison and judgment is optional."@en,
        "Read a positive integer n and process exactly n valid nonnegative integer values. For each x, invoke a separate factorial(x) function that receives x, calculates factorial using a loop and returns the result."@en,
        "Reject negative x with an error and request a replacement; rejected inputs do not count toward n. Calculate 0! = 1 and display each accepted result as x! = result."@en ;
    ns1:usesResource ns1:ER_Task405_Statement ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/eduknowgpt/OCSP/blob/main/CSP/cycles/cycle-04/en/TASK405-Factorial/TASK405-CSP-Report.md>,
        <https://github.com/eduknowgpt/OCSP/blob/main/CSP/cycles/cycle-04/en/TASK405-Factorial/TASK405-Factorial.md> .

ns1:LT_Task411 a ns1:LearningTask ;
    rdfs:label "Finding the Snake in a Grid learning task"@en ;
    ns1:hasAcquisitionContext ns1:AC_Task411 ;
    ns1:hasCompetenceActivation ns1:CA_Task411_CM02_Learning,
        ns1:CA_Task411_CM03_Learning,
        ns1:CA_Task411_CM04_Learning,
        ns1:CA_Task411_CM08_Learning,
        ns1:CA_Task411_CM14_Learning,
        ns1:CA_Task411_CM15_Learning ;
    ns1:hasInstructionalStatement "Assume exactly one valid, connected snake, without branches, loops or disconnected cells, with one head and tail. No invalid-grid validation or interactive input parser is required; the matrix may be supplied directly."@en,
        "Every body arrow points to its predecessor toward the head. Select an edge-adjacent body cell whose arrow points to the current cell; mere occupied adjacency is insufficient. The tail has no adjacent body cell pointing to it."@en,
        "For an arbitrary M x N rectangular matrix, locate h and return every snake cell exactly once from head to tail as zero-based [row, column] coordinates."@en,
        "Submit source code, coordinate sequences for both supplied examples, and a brief explanation of arrow-based selection and tail recognition. Rectangular-grid and boundary-head checks with explicit comparison and judgment are optional."@en ;
    ns1:usesResource ns1:ER_Task411_Statement ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/eduknowgpt/OCSP/blob/main/CSP/cycles/cycle-04/en/TASK411-Snake/TASK411-CSP-Report.md>,
        <https://github.com/eduknowgpt/OCSP/blob/main/CSP/cycles/cycle-04/en/TASK411-Snake/TASK411-Snake.md> .

